 "notes": "Default CIDR map values are not stated in the prompt so are not checked. Public vs private subnets are told apart via relationships (NAT, endpoints, DB subnet group) since names/tags are not stated. Endpoint SG checks: the HTTPS rule must be tcp (an all-protocol rule does not count); 'only within the VPC CIDR' is checked on the SG that carries the HTTPS-from-VPC rule (every egress CIDR is the VPC CIDR, no IPv6 egress), or on every separate egress rule. endpoint_sg now requires an endpoint to reference a security group (the old presence test passed on any SG; the duplicate endpoint_sg_used was removed). SG name must be the VPC name value + '-vpc-endpoints' (name or name_prefix). nat_private_route also accepts declared route tables/routes whose NAT reference goes through a local. subnet_azs: exactly two distinct AZs ('two default availability zones')."
